    "continuity": "If met: VB-07 — controlled standing attack. If not: return to catch, shorten distance, and lower net.",
    "bankLink": "Sport: Volleyball. Age: 12–14. Equipment: 12–16 balls, net or rope, 30 cones, bibs.\nTags: volleyball, court coverage, base position, team shape, net games, school PE.\nSkills: base positioning, recovery movement, court coverage, reading flight, calling, triangle shape.\nLoad: moderate. Complexity: intermediate.\nKeywords: base position, recover to base, court coverage, triangle shape, short ball, deep ball, filling the gap, movement between contacts.",
    "systemData": "Physical: moderate. Cognitive: moderate–high. Organizational: moderate. Independence: medium.",
    "teacherSummary": "State goal and cues.\nWarm up through movement and self-contact.\nBuild the skill without pressure.\nAdd a decision and small game.\nClose with evidence and next step.",
    "pedagogicalValue": "Why important? Volleyball is played mostly without touching the ball, and the difference between a team that covers the court and one that does not is positional habit rather than skill or speed.\nWhat develops? A defined base position and the discipline of recovering to it, movement that arrives early and balanced, spatial awareness of the gap a moving team-mate leaves, and the communication that assigns space rather than just claiming a ball.\nWhy not skip? Without taught coverage, three students stand in a line watching each other, easy balls land in gaps nobody owned, and the class concludes it is bad at volleyball when in fact it was simply standing in the wrong places.",
