    "bankLink": "Sport: Volleyball. Age: 12–14. Equipment: 12–16 balls, net or rope, 30 cones, bibs.\nTags: volleyball, net defence, blocking, backcourt coverage, net games, school PE.\nSkills: shadow block, hand position, side-step footwork, balanced landing, backcourt coverage, calling.\nLoad: moderate. Complexity: intermediate.\nKeywords: shadow block, hands high, land same side, net safety, backcourt coverage, block and cover, side-step footwork, taking one side.",
    "systemData": "Physical: moderate. Cognitive: moderate–high. Organizational: moderate. Independence: medium.",
    "teacherSummary": "State goal and cues.\nWarm up through movement and self-contact.\nBuild the skill without pressure.\nAdd a decision and small game.\nClose with evidence and next step.",
    "pedagogicalValue": "Why important? It is the first organised answer to an attack, and it teaches the principle that blocking and back-court defence are one coordinated act: the block decides where the ball can go, and the cover waits there.\nWhat develops? A safe blocking shape with high spread hands, side-step footwork along the net, a balanced landing on the same side, reading the attacker's hand, and the calling that pairs a blocker with a coverer.\nWhy not skip? The net is where the main collision risks in school volleyball sit — landing under it, reaching over it, or colliding with a team-mate — and the habits taught here address all three; without coverage, meanwhile, a block that deflects the ball simply wins the point for the other team.",
